From 54a5fa724331c1f08b0732ee3988987feaca5b11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vignesh Viswanathan <viswanat@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:19:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: share resident RW segments across firmware
 images

elf_fw_optimization currently shares only the segments before the
first RW program header of the second ELF ("RO segments") across
endpoints loading the identical firmware image. The FW team has
confirmed that some RW segments are also safe to share: a RW segment
is "resident" (copied once into endpoint SRAM by the device and
never written back to DDR) unless it is marked "pageable" or
"remote" via specific ELF p_flags bits. Only pageable/remote RW
segments are genuinely private per-endpoint and must keep getting
their own allocation. The ELF layout guarantees all resident RW
segments are contiguous and appear before any pageable/remote
segment, so the existing single-boundary design still applies -
only the stopping condition changes.

Add ELF_PFLAGS_PAGEABLE_MASK/VALUE and ELF_PFLAGS_REMOTE_MASK/VALUE
to identify pageable and remote RW segments via p_flags, and rework
mhi_analyze_elf_for_shared_segments() (renamed from
mhi_analyze_elf_for_ro_segments()) to scan all program headers in a
single pass: it now stops the shared boundary at the first RW
segment that is pageable or remote, tracking the maximum segment end
offset (max_end) along the way. If no pageable/remote RW segment is
found, the boundary falls back to max_end and the entire image is
treated as shareable, replacing the previous -EINVAL error for
"no RW segment found".

Since the shared region is no longer purely read-only, rename the
RO-specific identifiers to reflect the broader shared region:
struct mhi_shared_ro to struct mhi_shared_segments,
mhi_shared_ro_table to mhi_shared_segments_table,
mhi_shared_ro_lock to mhi_shared_segments_lock,
MHI_MAX_SHARED_RO_ENTRIES to MHI_MAX_SHARED_SEGMENT_ENTRIES,
mhi_save_shared_ro_segments() to mhi_save_shared_segments(), and
mhi_cntrl->shared_ro_segments to mhi_cntrl->shared_segments in
struct mhi_controller.

Change-Id: Iea5b2245821c874d21ba43c34fac0ba624cb2edb
Signed-off-by: Vignesh Viswanathan <viswanat@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
